exposed in `colHeight` board vocabulary: after the `L`, columns `c, c+1, c+2` read `f+1, f+1, f+2`.
That triple is exactly the S-notch convention `applyStep_S_skyline_noclear` consumes — two equal
columns `colHeight c = colHeight (c+1)` with a one-higher step `colHeight (c+2) = colHeight c + 1` —
