case of that frame: an `O` played on a flat pair `c, c+1` that is entirely separated from the notch
triple `nc, nc+1, nc+2` (`hsep : nc + 2 < c ∨ c + 1 < nc`) leaves all three notch column heights
exactly where they were. So a reserved S- or Z-notch at `nc` survives an `O` landing elsewhere on the
