/-- **All-five-flat pocket-fill dispatcher.** Consolidation of the five flat arbitrary-member fill
arcs (O, horizontal-I, T, L, J). For any one of those five pieces, dropping it on the guaranteed
width-four floor pocket of an arbitrary `IsLevelPocketBandAt standard 2 floor` member is a valid
placement landing in `IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline standard 2` (hence not lost). The five flat pieces are
exactly those that flush-fill a *level* pocket — unlike S and Z, none needs a staircase notch — so
this is the maximal piece set closed by a single uniform pocket drop. The proof case-splits the piece
hypothesis and dispatches to the matching per-piece arc. Bundling them is the first half of the
all-seven fill dispatcher (the S and Z phases additionally consume their `floorNotch` bricks). -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt {floor : ℕ} {b : Board}
    {p : Piece} (hp : p = Piece.O ∨ p = Piece.I ∨ p = Piece.T ∨ p = Piece.L ∨ p = Piece.J)
    (hb : IsLevelPocketBandAt GameConfig.standard 2 floor b) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid GameConfig.standard ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline GameConfig.standard 2
        (Placement.applyStep GameConfig.standard b pl) ∧
      ¬ Board.isLost GameConfig.standard
        (Placement.applyStep GameConfig.standard b pl) := by
  rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_O_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt hb
  · exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_horizI_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt hb
  · exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_T_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt hb
  · exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_L_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt hb
  · exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_J_pocket_of_isLevelPocketBandAt hb

