the spread) while the remaining four pocket columns `pc + 4, pc + 5, pc + 6, pc + 7` stay flat at
`base`, so the post-move board is again `IsLevelPocketBandAt standard 2 base` with the width-four
pocket regenerated from the pocket's own residual width at columns `pc + 4 .. pc + 7`. As the
widest footprint of the five flat pieces, the horizontal-`I` is the most width-hungry self-regen
arc — it needs the full width-eight pocket to leave a width-four remainder — but it is also the
gentlest riser (`+1` versus the `O`'s `+2`). Floor is fixed (`floor' = base`), so it slots into
`reservoirCarrier_fill_step` at zero ledger cost; like the `O` arc it discharges the `#89`
site-existence obligation for this single flat region input shape. -/
theorem isLevelPocketBandAt_horizI_lands_widePocket {base pc : ℕ} {h : ℕ → ℕ}
    (hslack : base + 2 ≤ GameConfig.standard.rows)
    (hw0 : h 0 = 0)
