/-- **Spread-preserving valley fill, J-shelf: a flat J dropped onto a floor-level
triple keeps the band width fixed.** The J member of the spread-non-increasing family,
mirror of the L valley fit. When the level triple `(c, c+1, c+2)` sits at the band
**floor** (`hcfloor : h c = floor`) and the band is at least two deep
(`hspread : 2 ≤ spread`), the J raises its left riser to `floor + 2 ≤ floor + spread` and
the two right columns to `floor + 1` — all inside the existing band — so the spread budget
