/-- **One level floor pocket absorbs EVERY flat-shelf piece at zero spread cost.** The
consolidation of the five flat-shelf valley fits (`O`, horizontal-`I`, `T`, `L`, `J`) into a
single existence statement: on a spread-`spread` band carrying a width-four LEVEL floor pocket
`(c, c+1, c+2, c+3)` off the reserved well (all four at `h c = floor`, band at least two deep),
ANY piece the adversary draws from the flat-shelf set `{O, I, T, L, J}` admits a placement that
satisfies the **full `hstep` triple** — correct piece, `pl.Valid cfg`, and a post-board that is
again a spread-`spread` band. Each branch seats the piece at the pocket origin `c`, discharges
validity from the column bounds via the matching `valid_*` lemma (`valid_O`/`valid_horizI`/
`valid_T`/`valid_L`/`valid_J`), and cites the matching per-piece valley atom — `O` at `rot 0`
(width two), horizontal-`I` at `rot 0` (width four, needs only `1 ≤ spread`), `T` at `rot 2`,
`L`/`J` at `rot 0` (width three) — so the spread never grows. This is the FIVE-piece half of
the phase-conditional carrier (only the staircase pieces `S`, `Z` still demand a notch, handled
on demand): with a guaranteed level four-pocket the bag's non-staircase draws are all absorbed
without widening the band, in exactly the shape `tetrisSolvableValid_of_spreadBand_closed`'s
`hstep` consumes. The genuine remaining content is supplying that pocket on a surface the player
MAINTAINS (the pocket-existence wall, crux #66), plus the `S`/`Z` notch companion. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hc3 : c + 3 < cfg.cols)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2)
    (hwc3 : w ≠ c + 3) (hw0 : h w = 0)
    (heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c) (heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c) (heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece)
    (hp : p = Piece.O ∨ p = Piece.I ∨ p = Piece.T ∨ p = Piece.L ∨ p = Piece.J) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.O, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_O hc1,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_O_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hw hwc hwc1 hw0
        heq1.symm hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩
  · exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.I, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_horizI hc3,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_horizI_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
        hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor (by omega) hband hslack⟩
  · exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.T, rot := 2, col := c }, rfl, valid_T hc2,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_T_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
        heq1 heq2 hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩
  · exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.L, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_L hc2,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_L_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
        heq1 heq2 hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩
  · exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.J, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_J hc2,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_J_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
        heq1 heq2 hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩

/-- **The refined invariant lands every flat-shelf piece (band-half of `hI_step`).**
Unpacking `IsLevelPocketBand`, its guaranteed level width-four pocket `(c, c+1, c+2, c+3)`
seated at the band floor is exactly the bundle
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket` consumes, so on a depth-at-least-two
pocket band ANY piece from the flat shelf `{O, I, T, L, J}` admits a VALID placement landing
back in a spread-`spread` band. This is the `{O, I, T, L, J}` half of the reachability route's
`hI_step` (`tetrisSolvableValid_of_strategy_invariant` at `I := IsLevelPocketBand`): the move
lands honestly in the wider band carrier — NOT yet back in a pocket band, since pocket
regeneration is the remaining obligation — but it pins down validity and a band result, so the
strategy σ can always answer a flat-shelf draw without losing the band bound. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand
    {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ} {b : Board}
    (hb : IsLevelPocketBand cfg spread b) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (p : Piece)
    (hp : p = Piece.O ∨ p = Piece.I ∨ p = Piece.T ∨ p = Piece.L ∨ p = Piece.J) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread (Placement.applyStep cfg b pl) := by
  obtain ⟨h, floor, w, c, rfl, hw, hw0, hband, hcap, hc3, hwc, hwc1, hwc2, hwc3,
    hcf, hc1f, hc2f, hc3f⟩ := hb
  exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket
    (by omega) (by omega) (by omega) hc3 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hwc3 hw0
    (by rw [hc1f, hcf]) (by rw [hc2f, hcf]) (by rw [hc3f, hcf]) hcf hspread hband hcap p hp

/-- **Flat-shelf survival face of the level-pocket-band landing.** The `not_isLost`
companion to `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand`: on a depth-at-least-two
level-pocket band, every flat-shelf piece `{O, I, T, L, J}` admits a VALID placement whose
landing board is not lost. Composes the band landing (which exits to a spread-`spread` band,
dropping the pocket) with the band survival certificate
(`not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline`, which reads the ceiling cap `floor + spread ≤ rows`
off the band itself). This is the survival half the reachability route's non-loss bookkeeping
consumes: whatever flat-shelf piece the adversary draws on a player-built pocket band, the
strategy σ answers it without topping out, independent of the (yet-unproven) pocket
regeneration. The flat-shelf analogue of the rich-surface
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_richStandard_not_isLost`. -/
theorem not_isLost_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand
    {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ} {b : Board}
    (hb : IsLevelPocketBand cfg spread b) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (p : Piece)
    (hp : p = Piece.O ∨ p = Piece.I ∨ p = Piece.T ∨ p = Piece.L ∨ p = Piece.J) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      ¬ Board.isLost cfg (Placement.applyStep cfg b pl) := by
  obtain ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, hband⟩ :=
    isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand hb hspread p hp
  exact ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline hband⟩

/-- **A flat top discharges the full hstep triple for EVERY flat-shelf piece.** The flat-top
specialisation of `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket`: on a reserved-well
flat top (every non-well column at the common height `base`, the well at `0`), the width-four
LEVEL pocket the consolidation needs always EXISTS by disjoint-quad pigeonhole (`8 ≤ cfg.cols`),
so the explicit-pocket hypotheses discharge and ANY piece from the flat-shelf set
`{O, I, T, L, J}` admits a placement meeting the FULL `hstep` triple — correct piece,
`pl.Valid cfg`, post-board a spread-`2` band. Viewing the flat top as a spread-`2` band
(`base ≤ h j ≤ base + 2` holds trivially, the four pocket columns level at `floor = base`), the
five-piece consolidation lands each piece without exceeding band width `2`. This is the flat-top
analogue of the per-piece `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_horizI_lands_of_isFlatTop`, now covering all
five flat pieces at once WITH validity — exactly the `{O, I, T, L, J}` branches of the flat-top
carrier closure, exiting (honestly) to the wider band the surface roughening produces, not back
to a flat top. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valid_lands_of_isFlatTop {cfg : GameConfig} {base w : ℕ}
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (h8 : 8 ≤ cfg.cols) (hslack : base + 2 ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece)
    (hp : p = Piece.O ∨ p = Piece.I ∨ p = Piece.T ∨ p = Piece.L ∨ p = Piece.J) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg 2
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg (fun j => if j = w then 0 else base)) pl) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc3, hwc, hwc1, hwc2, hwc3⟩ :
      ∃ c, c + 3 < cfg.cols ∧ w ≠ c ∧ w ≠ c + 1 ∧ w ≠ c + 2 ∧ w ≠ c + 3 := by
    rcases Nat.lt_or_ge w 4 with hlt | hge
    · exact ⟨4, by omega, by omega, by omega, by omega, by omega⟩
    · exact ⟨0, by omega, by omega, by omega, by omega, by omega⟩
  have hc : c < cfg.cols := by omega
  have hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols := by omega
  have hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols := by omega
  set h : ℕ → ℕ := fun j => if j = w then 0 else base with hh
  have hw0 : h w = 0 := by rw [hh]; simp
  have hbase : h c = base := by rw [hh]; simp only [if_neg (Ne.symm hwc)]
  have hbase1 : h (c + 1) = base := by rw [hh]; simp only [if_neg (Ne.symm hwc1)]
  have hbase2 : h (c + 2) = base := by rw [hh]; simp only [if_neg (Ne.symm hwc2)]
  have hbase3 : h (c + 3) = base := by rw [hh]; simp only [if_neg (Ne.symm hwc3)]
  have heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c := by rw [hbase1, hbase]
  have heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c := by rw [hbase2, hbase]
  have heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c := by rw [hbase3, hbase]
  have hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → base ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ base + 2 := by
    intro j hj hjw
    have hjb : h j = base := by rw [hh]; simp only [if_neg hjw]
    omega
  exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2
    hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hbase (by omega) hband hslack p hp

/-- **Spread-preserving valley fill, S-notch: a notch-seated S dropped onto a
floor-level staircase keeps the band width fixed.** The first notch-seated member of the
spread-non-increasing family (companion to the flat-shelf O, horizontal-I, T, L, J valley
fits). Unlike those, S needs a staircase `(h c = h (c+1), h (c+2) = h c + 1)`; when that
staircase base sits at the band floor (`hcfloor : h c = floor`) and the band is at least two
deep (`hspread : 2 ≤ spread`), the S lands flush — profile `(floor, floor, floor+1) ↦
(floor+1, floor+2, floor+2)` — every touched column staying inside `[floor, floor+spread]`,
so the spread budget is unchanged. This is the S analogue of absorbing the bag's forced
hole-maker into a floor pocket at zero spread cost; only the mirror Z notch remains. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_S_valley_of_isSpreadBounded {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2)
    (hw0 : h w = 0)
    (heq : h c = h (c + 1)) (hstep : h (c + 2) = h c + 1)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows) :
    IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
      (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h)
        { piece := Piece.S, rot := 0, col := c }) := by
  rw [applyStep_S_skyline_noclear hc hc1 hc2 heq hstep hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0]
  refine ⟨Function.update (Function.update (Function.update h c (h c + 1))
      (c + 1) (h c + 2)) (c + 2) (h c + 2), floor, w, rfl, hw, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Function.update_of_ne hwc2, Function.update_of_ne hwc1,
        Function.update_of_ne hwc]; exact hw0
  · intro j hj hjw
    rcases eq_or_ne j (c + 2) with rfl | hjc2'
    · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
    · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc2']
      rcases eq_or_ne j (c + 1) with rfl | hjc1'
      · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
      · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc1']
        rcases eq_or_ne j c with rfl | hjc'
        · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
        · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc']
          obtain ⟨hjlo, hjhi⟩ := hband j hj hjw
          omega
  · exact hslack

/-- **Spread-preserving valley fill, Z-notch: a notch-seated Z dropped onto a
floor-level mirror staircase keeps the band width fixed.** The exact mirror of the S valley
fit, and the seventh and final piece of the spread-non-increasing family. Z needs the mirror
staircase `(h (c+1) = h (c+2), h c = h (c+1) + 1)` — the left column one higher — so the two
equal **right** columns are the staircase base; seat that base at the band floor
(`hcfloor : h (c+1) = floor`) with the band at least two deep (`hspread : 2 ≤ spread`), and the
Z lands flush — profile `(floor+1, floor, floor) ↦ (floor+2, floor+2, floor+1)` — every touched
column staying inside `[floor, floor+spread]`, so the spread budget is unchanged. With this brick
**all seven** tetromino shapes admit a zero spread-cost valley fit: every piece the bag can force
can be absorbed into a floor pocket or staircase without widening the band. The remaining content
is the pocket/notch *existence* lemma (a sufficiently full band always offers such a landing site)
and the per-bag scheduling between valley fills and the well-clearing descent. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_Z_valley_of_isSpreadBounded {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2)
    (hw0 : h w = 0)
    (heq : h (c + 1) = h (c + 2)) (hstep : h c = h (c + 1) + 1)
    (hcfloor : h (c + 1) = floor) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows) :
    IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
      (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h)
        { piece := Piece.Z, rot := 0, col := c }) := by
  rw [applyStep_Z_skyline_noclear hc hc1 hc2 heq hstep hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0]
  refine ⟨Function.update (Function.update (Function.update h c (h (c + 1) + 2))
      (c + 1) (h (c + 1) + 2)) (c + 2) (h (c + 1) + 1), floor, w, rfl, hw, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Function.update_of_ne hwc2, Function.update_of_ne hwc1,
        Function.update_of_ne hwc]; exact hw0
  · intro j hj hjw
    rcases eq_or_ne j (c + 2) with rfl | hjc2'
    · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
    · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc2']
      rcases eq_or_ne j (c + 1) with rfl | hjc1'
      · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
      · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc1']
        rcases eq_or_ne j c with rfl | hjc'
        · rw [Function.update_self]; omega
        · rw [Function.update_of_ne hjc']
          obtain ⟨hjlo, hjhi⟩ := hband j hj hjw
          omega
  · exact hslack

/-- **The notch companion: a piece-dispatched `{S, Z}` valley fit, spread-preserving.**
The `{S, Z}` analogue of `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket`. S and Z
do not fit a flat shelf — each needs its own floor staircase (S the right-riser
`h c = h (c+1), h (c+2) = h c + 1`; Z the mirror left-riser
`h (c+1) = h (c+2), h c = h (c+1) + 1`), so the notch hypothesis is dispatched on the piece
rather than shared. Given the band data plus the staircase appropriate to `p`, the seated
piece lands flush at zero spread cost (the touched columns stay inside `[floor, floor+spread]`),
yielding a VALID placement landing back in a spread-`spread` band. This is the `{S, Z}` half of
the reachability route's `hI_step` companion to the flat-shelf
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand`: once the strategy has built the
piece-appropriate notch, the forced S or Z is absorbed without widening the band. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2)
    (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece) (hp : p = Piece.S ∨ p = Piece.Z)
    (hSnotch : p = Piece.S → h c = h (c + 1) ∧ h (c + 2) = h c + 1 ∧ h c = floor)
    (hZnotch : p = Piece.Z → h (c + 1) = h (c + 2) ∧ h c = h (c + 1) + 1 ∧ h (c + 1) = floor) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  rcases hp with rfl | rfl
  · obtain ⟨heq, hstep, hcfloor⟩ := hSnotch rfl
    exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.S, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_S hc2,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_S_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
        heq hstep hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩
  · obtain ⟨heq, hstep, hcfloor⟩ := hZnotch rfl
    exact ⟨{ piece := Piece.Z, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_Z hc2,
      isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_Z_valley_of_isSpreadBounded hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
        heq hstep hcfloor hspread hband hslack⟩

/-- **Staircase survival face of the `{S, Z}` valley fit.** The `not_isLost` companion to
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch`, mirroring the flat-shelf
`not_isLost_lands_of_isLevelPocketBand`: on a depth-at-least-two spread band carrying the
`p`-appropriate floor staircase (S the right-riser, Z the mirror left-riser), the forced
staircase piece admits a VALID placement whose landing board is not lost. Composes the
spread-preserving valley fit (which keeps the band width at `spread`) with the band survival
certificate `not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline`. Together with the flat-shelf face this
closes the per-piece non-loss certificate for ALL seven pieces on a player-built band — the
survival bookkeeping the reachability route threads through each σ-move. -/
theorem not_isLost_SZ_valley_of_notch {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2)
    (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece) (hp : p = Piece.S ∨ p = Piece.Z)
    (hSnotch : p = Piece.S → h c = h (c + 1) ∧ h (c + 2) = h c + 1 ∧ h c = floor)
    (hZnotch : p = Piece.Z → h (c + 1) = h (c + 2) ∧ h c = h (c + 1) + 1 ∧ h (c + 1) = floor) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      ¬ Board.isLost cfg (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  obtain ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, hband'⟩ :=
    isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0 hspread
      hband hslack p hp hSnotch hZnotch
  exact ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline hband'⟩

/-- **The complete valley menu: a fully equipped band absorbs all seven pieces at the
band width.** The capstone of the spread-non-increasing family, consolidating
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket` (the five flat-shelf pieces seated
at a width-four level pocket `c..c+3`) and `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch`
(the two staircase pieces seated at a separate notch site `d..d+2`) into a single `∀ p`
dispatch: given a spread band that simultaneously offers a level floor pocket at `c` and
the `p`-appropriate staircase at `d`, WHATEVER tetromino the adversary draws lands a valid
placement back in a band of the SAME spread. The two landing sites are necessarily distinct
(a level pocket has equal heights, a staircase has a unit step), and carrying both at once
plus the well overflows the ten-column budget — so this menu is consumed phase-conditionally,
the surface presenting only the sites the still-owed pieces require. This is the per-piece
absorption oracle a scheduler calls; the open content is no longer WHICH placement answers a
draw, but MAINTAINING the needed sites across a bag. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_notch {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c d : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hc3 : c + 3 < cfg.cols)
    (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2) (hwc3 : w ≠ c + 3)
    (heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c) (heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c) (heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor)
    (hd : d < cfg.cols) (hd1 : d + 1 < cfg.cols) (hd2 : d + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwd : w ≠ d) (hwd1 : w ≠ d + 1) (hwd2 : w ≠ d + 2)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece)
    (hSnotch : p = Piece.S → h d = h (d + 1) ∧ h (d + 2) = h d + 1 ∧ h d = floor)
    (hZnotch : p = Piece.Z → h (d + 1) = h (d + 2) ∧ h d = h (d + 1) + 1 ∧ h (d + 1) = floor) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  cases p with
  | O =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.O (Or.inl rfl)
  | I =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.I (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))
  | T =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.T
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl)))
  | L =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.L
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))))
  | J =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.J
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr rfl))))
  | S =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch hd hd1 hd2 hw hwd hwd1 hwd2 hw0 hspread
      hband hslack Piece.S (Or.inl rfl) hSnotch hZnotch
  | Z =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch hd hd1 hd2 hw hwd hwd1 hwd2 hw0 hspread
      hband hslack Piece.Z (Or.inr rfl) hSnotch hZnotch

/-- **The complete two-notch valley menu: a band with a pocket AND both staircase notches absorbs
all seven pieces.** Strengthens `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_notch`, whose single
notch site `d` could serve only ONE of the two staircase pieces (an ascending site cannot also be a
descending one). Here the ascending `S`-notch lives at `d..d+2` and the descending `Z`-notch at its
own site `e..e+2`, so WHATEVER tetromino the adversary draws lands a valid placement inside the same
spread band: the five flat-shelf pieces seat at the width-four level pocket `c..c+3`, `S` at `d`, and
`Z` at `e`. The three sites may overlap freely (each piece touches only its own), subject only to the
shared reserved well `w` staying clear and the band invariant holding off-well. This is the genuine
all-seven closure the phase-conditional witnesses approximated one staircase at a time, and the
engine behind a single standard board closed under every adversarial next piece. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c d e : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hc3 : c + 3 < cfg.cols)
    (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2) (hwc3 : w ≠ c + 3)
    (heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c) (heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c) (heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor)
    (hd : d < cfg.cols) (hd1 : d + 1 < cfg.cols) (hd2 : d + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwd : w ≠ d) (hwd1 : w ≠ d + 1) (hwd2 : w ≠ d + 2)
    (hSnotch : h d = h (d + 1) ∧ h (d + 2) = h d + 1 ∧ h d = floor)
    (he : e < cfg.cols) (he1 : e + 1 < cfg.cols) (he2 : e + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwe : w ≠ e) (hwe1 : w ≠ e + 1) (hwe2 : w ≠ e + 2)
    (hZnotch : h (e + 1) = h (e + 2) ∧ h e = h (e + 1) + 1 ∧ h (e + 1) = floor)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline cfg spread
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  cases p with
  | O =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.O (Or.inl rfl)
  | I =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.I (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))
  | T =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.T
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl)))
  | L =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.L
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))))
  | J =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_flat5_valley_of_levelPocket hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1
      hwc2 hwc3 hw0 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor hspread hband hslack Piece.J
      (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr rfl))))
  | S =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch hd hd1 hd2 hw hwd hwd1 hwd2 hw0 hspread
      hband hslack Piece.S (Or.inl rfl) (fun _ => hSnotch) (fun hpZ => absurd hpZ (by decide))
  | Z =>
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_SZ_valley_of_notch he he1 he2 hw hwe hwe1 hwe2 hw0 hspread
      hband hslack Piece.Z (Or.inr rfl) (fun hpS => absurd hpS (by decide)) (fun _ => hZnotch)

/-- **The two-notch valley menu survives every adversarial next piece, at ANY floor.** The non-loss
face of `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch`, composed with
`not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline` (every spread-bounded reserved-well board sits under the
ceiling). From any band that offers a width-four level pocket, an ascending `S`-notch, a descending
`Z`-notch, and a reserved well, WHATEVER piece the adversary draws admits a valid placement whose
landing board is not lost. Unlike `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_standard_not_isLost`, this is
floor-agnostic: it survives at the lowered floors produced after an I-clear reset, so it is the
reusable survival face the eventual two-phase strategy quotes whenever the band carrier re-enters an
all-seven-ready surface at whatever height the clear left behind. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch_not_isLost
    {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c d e : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hc3 : c + 3 < cfg.cols)
    (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2) (hwc3 : w ≠ c + 3)
    (heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c) (heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c) (heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor)
    (hd : d < cfg.cols) (hd1 : d + 1 < cfg.cols) (hd2 : d + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwd : w ≠ d) (hwd1 : w ≠ d + 1) (hwd2 : w ≠ d + 2)
    (hSnotch : h d = h (d + 1) ∧ h (d + 2) = h d + 1 ∧ h d = floor)
    (he : e < cfg.cols) (he1 : e + 1 < cfg.cols) (he2 : e + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwe : w ≠ e) (hwe1 : w ≠ e + 1) (hwe2 : w ≠ e + 2)
    (hZnotch : h (e + 1) = h (e + 2) ∧ h e = h (e + 1) + 1 ∧ h (e + 1) = floor)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      ¬ Board.isLost cfg (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  obtain ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, hband'⟩ :=
    isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch
      hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hwc hwc1 hwc2 hwc3 heq1 heq2 heq3 hcfloor
      hd hd1 hd2 hwd hwd1 hwd2 hSnotch he he1 he2 hwe hwe1 hwe2 hZnotch
      hw hw0 hspread hband hslack p
  exact ⟨pl, hpiece, hvalid, not_isLost_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline hband'⟩

/-- **The two-notch valley menu lands every piece at a PINNED floor.** The floor-magnitude-tracking
upgrade of `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch`: same single-board geometry
(reserved well `w`, width-four level pocket at `c..c+3`, ascending `S`-notch at `d..d+2`, descending
`Z`-notch at `e..e+2`, all sitting at `floor`), but the landing board is reported in the
floor-PINNED predicate `IsSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt cfg spread floor` rather than the existential
`IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline`. Dispatch is the pinned per-piece atom set: O/I/T/L/J seat in the level
pocket via the `..._flat_at` atoms, `S` in its ascending notch and `Z` in its descending notch via the
`..._notch_at` atoms — every one concluding at the SAME pinned floor, so the carrier ledger
(`base + spread + T.card + 1 ≤ rows`) stays available across the step. This is the magnitude-tracking
brick the iter603 frontier docstring flagged as missing: the existential menu plus the
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_of_isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline` bridge recover only floor EXISTENCE, losing
the floor value the reservoir ledger needs. It is NOT the closure: it is a from-surface menu that
still requires the caller to supply pocket + S-notch + Z-notch sites at the floor; cross-step
site-regeneration and the all-orders per-bag accounting (crux #66/#72) remain open, and
`TetrisSolvableValid` is NOT proven. No sorry. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_all7_valley_of_pocket_Snotch_Znotch {cfg : GameConfig} {spread : ℕ}
    {h : ℕ → ℕ} {floor w c d e : ℕ}
    (hc : c < cfg.cols) (hc1 : c + 1 < cfg.cols) (hc2 : c + 2 < cfg.cols) (hc3 : c + 3 < cfg.cols)
    (hwc : w ≠ c) (hwc1 : w ≠ c + 1) (hwc2 : w ≠ c + 2) (hwc3 : w ≠ c + 3)
    (heq1 : h (c + 1) = h c) (heq2 : h (c + 2) = h c) (heq3 : h (c + 3) = h c)
    (hcfloor : h c = floor)
    (hd : d < cfg.cols) (hd1 : d + 1 < cfg.cols) (hd2 : d + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwd : w ≠ d) (hwd1 : w ≠ d + 1) (hwd2 : w ≠ d + 2)
    (hSnotch : h d = h (d + 1) ∧ h (d + 2) = h d + 1 ∧ h d = floor)
    (he : e < cfg.cols) (he1 : e + 1 < cfg.cols) (he2 : e + 2 < cfg.cols)
    (hwe : w ≠ e) (hwe1 : w ≠ e + 1) (hwe2 : w ≠ e + 2)
    (hZnotch : h (e + 1) = h (e + 2) ∧ h e = h (e + 1) + 1 ∧ h (e + 1) = floor)
    (hw : w < cfg.cols) (hw0 : h w = 0) (hspread : 2 ≤ spread)
    (hband : ∀ j < cfg.cols, j ≠ w → floor ≤ h j ∧ h j ≤ floor + spread)
    (hslack : floor + spread ≤ cfg.rows)
    (p : Piece) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid cfg ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt cfg spread floor
        (Placement.applyStep cfg (skyline cfg h) pl) := by
  cases p with
  | O =>
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.O, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_O hc1, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_O_flat_at hc hc1 hw hwc hwc1 hw0
      hcfloor (heq1.trans hcfloor) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega) hslack
  | I =>
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.I, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_horizI hc3, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_horizI_flat_at hc hc1 hc2 hc3 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hwc3 hw0
      hcfloor (heq1.trans hcfloor) (heq2.trans hcfloor) (heq3.trans hcfloor) hband (le_refl floor)
      (by omega) hslack
  | T =>
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.T, rot := 2, col := c }, rfl, valid_T hc2, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_T_flat_at hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
      hcfloor (heq1.trans hcfloor) (heq2.trans hcfloor) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega) hslack
  | L =>
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.L, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_L hc2, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_L_flat_at hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
      hcfloor (heq1.trans hcfloor) (heq2.trans hcfloor) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega) hslack
  | J =>
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.J, rot := 0, col := c }, rfl, valid_J hc2, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_J_flat_at hc hc1 hc2 hw hwc hwc1 hwc2 hw0
      hcfloor (heq1.trans hcfloor) (heq2.trans hcfloor) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega) hslack
  | S =>
    obtain ⟨hSeq1, hSeq2, hSfloor⟩ := hSnotch
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.S, rot := 0, col := d }, rfl, valid_S hd2, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_S_notch_at hd hd1 hd2 hw hwd hwd1 hwd2 hw0
      hSfloor (hSeq1.symm.trans hSfloor) (by rw [hSeq2, hSfloor]) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega)
      hslack
  | Z =>
    obtain ⟨hZeq1, hZeq2, hZfloor⟩ := hZnotch
    refine ⟨{ piece := Piece.Z, rot := 0, col := e }, rfl, valid_Z he2, ?_⟩
    exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkylineAt_applyStep_Z_notch_at he he1 he2 hw hwe hwe1 hwe2 hw0
      (by rw [hZeq2, hZfloor]) hZfloor (hZeq1.symm.trans hZfloor) hband (le_refl floor) (by omega)
      hslack

/-- **The phase-conditional landing surface is realizable in ten standard columns.** A concrete
witness that the single-notch carrier geometry — reserved well, ONE staircase notch, and a
width-four level pocket — fits inside `GameConfig.standard`'s ten columns with room to spare. The
surface is `h = (0, 4, 4, 5, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4)`: well at column `0`, an S-notch at columns `1..3`
(heights `4, 4, 5`), and a level pocket at columns `4..7` (all `4`), leaving columns `8, 9` as flat
filler. It is a spread-`2` reserved-well band (off-well heights lie in `[4, 6]`), so for EVERY drawn
piece other than `Z` the all-seven valley menu lands a valid placement keeping the spread-`2` band:
the five flat-shelf pieces seat in the pocket and `S` seats in the notch, while `Z` is excluded by
hypothesis because its mirror notch is absent.

This corrects the earlier `1 + 4 + 3 + 3 = 11 > 10` infeasibility reading (task `#90`), which double
counted two simultaneous staircase notches: a phase that owes only one staircase piece needs only
one notch, and `well(1) + notch(3) + pocket(4) = 8 ≤ 10`. It is the positive feasibility witness the
phase-conditional carrier (`#91`) is built on — the concrete from-surface a future S-phase `hstep`
quotes, with the matching `Z`-phase mirror obtained by reflection. -/
theorem isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_Sphase_valley_standard (p : Piece) (hp : p ≠ Piece.Z) :
    ∃ pl : Placement, pl.piece = p ∧ pl.Valid GameConfig.standard ∧
      IsSpreadBoundedRWSkyline GameConfig.standard 2
        (Placement.applyStep GameConfig.standard
          (skyline GameConfig.standard
            (fun j => if j = 0 then 0 else if j = 3 then 5 else 4)) pl) := by
  have hband : ∀ j < GameConfig.standard.cols, j ≠ 0 →
      (4 : ℕ) ≤ (fun j => if j = 0 then 0 else if j = 3 then 5 else 4) j ∧
      (fun j => if j = 0 then 0 else if j = 3 then 5 else 4) j ≤ 4 + 2 := by
    intro j hj hjw
    have hj10 : j < 10 := hj
    interval_cases j <;> revert hjw <;> decide
  exact isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_all7_valley_of_pocket_notch
    (c := 4) (d := 1) (w := 0) (floor := 4) (spread := 2)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
    hband (by decide)
    p (fun _ => by decide) (fun hpZ => absurd hpZ hp)

/-- **The Z-phase mirror landing surface, realizable in ten standard columns.** The reflection
partner of `isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_Sphase_valley_standard`: the same single-notch carrier geometry
