/-- **Column-budget obstruction: a pocket, both staircase notches, and a reserved well cannot
coexist in ten columns.** The rigorous form of the informal `1 + 4 + 3 + 3 = 11 > 10` reading
(task `#90`). If a width-four level pocket `[c, c+4)`, an `S`-notch `[d, d+3)`, a `Z`-notch
`[e, e+3)`, and a reserved well `[w, w+1)` are pairwise column-disjoint and all contained in
`[0, 10)` — the standard column count — the four footprints demand `4 + 3 + 3 + 1 = 11` distinct
columns, exceeding the ten available, so no such arrangement exists (`False`).

This is the precise sense in which the single-reserved-well band carrier **cannot** be made closed
under an adversarial next piece while BOTH staircase pieces are still owed: to absorb whichever
piece the bag names next without leaving the band, the surface would need a flat pocket (for a
flat-shelf piece), an ascending notch (for `S`), a descending notch (for `Z`), and the empty well
(for the height-regulating `I`) all at once — and they do not fit. It is the negative companion to
`isSpreadBoundedRWSkyline_{S,Z}phase_valley_standard`, which show that with only ONE notch (one
staircase piece pending) the budget is `well + notch + pocket = 8 ≤ 10` and the surface IS
realizable. Together they pin the feasibility boundary exactly at the both-pending phase, forcing
the phase-conditional or staircase-pairing resolution (task `#91`). -/
theorem no_pocket_SZnotch_well_in_ten_cols
    (c d e w : ℕ)
    (hpocket : c + 4 ≤ 10) (hSnotch : d + 3 ≤ 10) (hZnotch : e + 3 ≤ 10) (hwell : w + 1 ≤ 10)
    (h_cd : c + 4 ≤ d ∨ d + 3 ≤ c) (h_ce : c + 4 ≤ e ∨ e + 3 ≤ c)
    (h_cw : c + 4 ≤ w ∨ w + 1 ≤ c) (h_de : d + 3 ≤ e ∨ e + 3 ≤ d)
    (h_dw : d + 3 ≤ w ∨ w + 1 ≤ d) (h_ew : e + 3 ≤ w ∨ w + 1 ≤ e) :
    False := by omega

